# The Dry Sifter's block faces, plus the hashish item.
#
# PLACEHOLDER art. Warlon Mhite may redraw these; that is what the .mctex is for.
#
# Palettes are sampled from the mod's own existing textures, not invented, so the block sits next
# to hemp planks and hemp canvas without either looking out of place:
#
#   wood    from block/hemp_planks   (5A5236 .. A89D73)
#   canvas  from item/hemp_canvas    (262417 .. D6CB90)
#   resin   from item/decarboxylated_hemp, warmed towards blond for loose kief
#
# The side face is the crafting recipe read literally — plank frame, canvas screen through the
# middle, plank frame — which is also what the block is. Block faces are deliberately low contrast
# (vanilla blocks span a median 76 luminance steps against an item's 164); the hashish item is not.

@palette wood
. = none
1 = 3F3A26      seam, darker than any plank tone so the courses read
2 = 5A5236
3 = 67603E
4 = 82794E
5 = 8A8155
6 = 948A5E
7 = A1976C
c = 5F5A3B      canvas shadow
d = 827B4E      canvas midtone
e = A39C6A      canvas light
f = D6CB90      canvas highlight

# Outer wall: two courses of planks with the screen's edge showing between them.
@texture block/dry_sifter_side 16x16 type=block tiling=true
6567777767777763
6655345666556644
5666565444455663
3223321122121121
6747777477765546
1111111111111111
cdcdcdcdcdcdcdcd
dfdfdfdfdfdfdfdf
cdcdcdcdcdcdcdcd
dfdfdfdfdfdfdfdf
1111111111111111
