# The screen itself — a plain weave seen through the open top, with the warp passing over the weft
# and back under it every two pixels. Each thread is two pixels wide but shaded across its width, so
# no 2x2 square is one flat colour; a mesh drawn as flat 2x2 blocks is an 8x8 drawing scaled up, and
# it moires badly the moment the block is more than a few metres away.
@texture block/dry_sifter_screen 16x16 type=block tiling=true
edffedffedffedff
edccedccedccedcc
ffedffedffedffed
ccedccedccedcced
edffedffedffedff
edccedccedccedcc
ffedffedffedffed
ccedccedccedcced
edffedffedffedff
edccedccedccedcc
ffedffedffedffed
ccedccedccedcced
edffedffedffedff
edccedccedccedcc
ffedffedffedffed
ccedccedccedcced

@palette resin
. = none
1 = 4A3E1E      shadowed kief
2 = 6E5C2C
3 = 9A8140
4 = C0A257
5 = D9BC72      blond highlight — trichome heads catch the light
a = 241A0C      pressed hash, darkest
b = 3A2A12
c = 4E3818
d = 664A21
e = 7E5D2B

# Loose kief piling up on the screen. Granular, not smooth: the point is that it is a powder.
